NAME
       pvchange - change settings of physical volumes

SYNOPSIS
       pvchange [-x y|n] [-u] PV...

DESCRIPTION
       pvchange changes properties of a physical volume that is already in
       use, for example whether LVM may place new extents on it.

OPTIONS
       -x, --allocatable y|n
              Allow (y) or forbid (n) new extents on this PV. Existing data
              stays where it is.

       -u, --uuid
              Give the PV a new random UUID.

EXAMPLES
       Keep new logical volumes off /dev/vdb1:

           pvchange -x n /dev/vdb1

SEE ALSO
       pvs(8), pvmove(8), lvm(8)
